# Copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; never commit a real key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here is required. Every feature below degrades to a working, honest
# version of itself when its variable is unset — a submission is never turned
# away because a deployment is missing an environment variable.
#
# Used by:
#   scripts/describe-bots.mjs   writes our own summary for each bot
#   scripts/map-jobs.mjs        proposes which jobs a bot fits
#   /api/submit                 drafts a listing from a submitted share link
#
# Unset: a submitted bot link is still fetched, checked and stored — a person
# writes it up instead. The validator gates what reaches the site either way.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Optional. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Only needed if your API key is identity-linked (the API will say so).
# Console > Settings > Workspaces — the id is in the URL.
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=wrkspc_...

# --- Submissions -------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Unset, a drafted record is kept on the submission and written with
# `pnpm queue --write` — the local equivalent of the pull request below. Set,
# submissions arrive as PRs instead, which is nicer once volume justifies it.
#
# Nobody submitting ever needs a GitHub account. This is only about where an
# accepted submission lands.
#
# The token belongs to a SEPARATE bot account and needs contents:write on that
# account's FORK only — never on this repo. A leaked token then vandalises a
# fork nobody reads: it cannot touch main, cannot merge, cannot rewrite history.
# SUBMIT_GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...
# SUBMIT_FORK=botjobs-bot/botjobs
# SUBMIT_UPSTREAM=lureilly1/botjobs

# Where submission state and rate-limit counters live. Point this OUTSIDE the
# repo in production so user input can never be committed.
# DATA_DIR=/var/lib/botjobs

# Salt for hashing submitter IPs. We count them, we do not store them.
# IP_SALT=change-me

# --- Analytics ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side, no client JavaScript and no cookies. Events land in
# $DATA_DIR/events.jsonl; read them with `pnpm stats`.
# Optional: also forward to PostHog. Unset = the local log is the whole system.
# POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...
# POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com
